1
00:00:03,198 --> 00:00:07,643
To turn the setup of one site into a recipe for another, open

2
00:00:07,643 --> 00:00:11,424
Configuration, Import and Export, Deployment Plans.

3
00:00:11,424 --> 00:00:13,878
Add a plan, and give it a name.

4
00:00:14,329 --> 00:00:15,672
Click Add Step.

5
00:00:15,672 --> 00:00:19,892
Each step is a kind of setup you can export, such as content

6
00:00:19,892 --> 00:00:23,026
types, settings, roles, users or templates.

7
00:00:23,026 --> 00:00:26,159
Add the steps you want, here all the roles.

8
00:00:26,609 --> 00:00:31,636
Add the users step too, to carry the people of the site, then check the plan.

9
00:00:31,636 --> 00:00:35,331
A step can have options of its own, and a plan can have

10
00:00:35,331 --> 00:00:37,269
as many steps as it needs.

11
00:00:37,720 --> 00:00:41,402
Click Execute, and choose to export the plan to a file.

12
00:00:41,402 --> 00:00:45,386
The file is a recipe that you can import on another site, in

13
00:00:45,386 --> 00:00:47,920
the JSON Import editor you just saw.

